  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the minimum probability of each lottery, which corresponds to the smallest probability assigned to any outcome. In both lotteries, the minimum probability is the chance of winning the positive amount (34% for A, 33% for B). The individual’s verbal report highlights a preference for the higher chance of winning something (i.e., the 34% vs 33%), which aligns directly with the information used by the decision reason. Furthermore, the individual’s justification—valuing the increased probability of winning over the slightly higher amount—matches the rule of the decision reason, which selects the lottery with the higher minimum probability. Although the individual does not use the term 'minimum probability,' the cognitive process described corresponds closely to the logic of the reason. Therefore, both the information considered and the justification align with the decision reason.",
